3. Motion ofFluid domain
The equations of motion (67), (68), (A.3) and (A.12) to (A.17) involve the displacement field uD, which describes how the region—or domain—which contains F, is deformed in time, cf. Fig.A.1. We will denote this region as the D. We observe that this field has, so far, been left arbitrary, and we have the freedom to choose it.
